  <data name="changelogTitle"><value>What's new</value></data>
  <data name="changelogBody"><value>1.3.0 — Oct 22, 2026 — Help sheet replaced by a structured Apple Help Book with search (macOS).
1.2.7 — Oct 22, 2026 — Third system languages show English; `;` also separates port lists.
1.2.6 — Live results on both platforms; harvest ghosts gain MAC, DNS, NetBIOS and UPnP clues; theme-aware header underline; running spinner.
1.2.5 — Results land live (Windows): per-chunk hostname merges, hard deadlines on resolver lookups.
1.2.4 — Size-to-fit button works again (macOS).
1.2.3 — Size-to-fit button + Cmd+Shift+F (macOS).
1.2.2 — Excel-style column resize (Windows).
1.2.1 — Double-click a header to size its column (both).
1.2.0 — Full parity: sort, filter, editable ports/timeouts, clickable services, vendor/type columns.
1.1.0 — Editable ports/timeouts, sort + filter, readable self-highlight; Windows gains Mica, menu bar, tabular results, installer.
1.0.0 — First stable release.
0.10.0 — Settings: language override, font size + mono, theme.
0.9.0 — Help and About sheets; EN/IT audit.
0.8.4 — Legend covers the computer icon.
0.8.3 — Legend covers randomized MACs; wider IP column.
0.8.2 — Wider start/end IP fields.
0.8.1 — Self-highlight survives the ARP refresh.
0.8.0 — Editable scan range + Get IP.
0.7.2 — Scanning host IP in yellow.
0.7.1 — HTTP names the software: HTTP/Caddy (80).
0.7.0 — All lookups overlap; wall time ≈ slowest pass.
0.6.3 — Randomized MACs flagged, never blamed; self row bold.
0.6.2 — Full IEEE OUI table (40k vendors), works offline.
0.6.1 — HTTP Server header as brand fallback on 80/8080.
0.6.0 — Scanning host always listed; more vendors, hints, mDNS types.
0.5.3 — Non-padded MAC groups parsed.
0.5.2 — CIDR skips .0/.255; a /24 probes 254 hosts.
0.5.1 — TTL 255 means embedded stacks, not routers; only 128 hints Windows.
0.5.0 — Radar-sweep app icon.
0.4.3 — Stable brand colors; device-type legend.
0.4.2 — Device-type color dot; generic Linux TTL guess dropped.
0.4.1 — Hostnames fixed: `.local` queries, A records, NetBIOS.
0.4.0 — Fewer missing MACs (re-ping + ARP re-read); TTL hints.
0.3.0 — ICMP ping sweep + TCP fallback; Wi-Fi-tuned ports/timeouts.
0.2.1 — Header/row alignment; OUI lookup fix.
0.2.0 — Vendor/Type column; 4× faster discovery; progressive results.
0.1.0 — Skeleton: targets, TCP discovery, port sweep, ARP MACs, reverse DNS, CSV, EN/IT.</value></data>
  <data name="helpSearchHint"><value>Search help…</value></data>
  <data name="helpChScanTitle"><value>Scanning the network</value></data>
  <data name="helpChScanBody"><value>Enter a start and end IP and press Start (Return works too). Get IP fills this machine's subnet range. Ranges accept CIDR (192.168.1.0/24) and full or last-octet forms; .0 and .255 are never probed. Discovery ping plus TCP probes run in parallel; the bar tracks progress, the spinner marks a running scan. Stop keeps the rows found so far.</value></data>
  <data name="helpChResultsTitle"><value>Reading the results</value></data>
  <data name="helpChResultsBody"><value>One row per live host appears the moment it answers. Click a header to sort (again to reverse); the filter narrows the list; drag a boundary gripper — or double-click it — to size a column. HTTP/HTTPS services open in the browser. Export saves the visible rows as CSV, disabled while a scan runs.</value></data>
  <data name="helpChLegendTitle"><value>Colors and icons</value></data>
  <data name="helpChLegendBody"><value>The dot before each IP is the device type (legend below the table); each brand gets its own stable color. A shuffle icon marks a randomized MAC, which carries no vendor. This PC is bold with a computer icon and accent IP.</value></data>
  <data name="helpChNamesTitle"><value>MACs, vendors and hostnames</value></data>
  <data name="helpChNamesBody"><value>MACs come from the local ARP table, refreshed after discovery with a targeted re-ping for gaps. The vendor is the OUI prefix; the HTTP Server header or the UPnP description fills the brand slot when it is silent. Names come from mDNS, NetBIOS, then reverse DNS; harvest-only ghosts get the full treatment too.</value></data>
  <data name="helpChSettingsTitle"><value>Settings and troubleshooting</value></data>
  <data name="helpChSettingsBody"><value>Settings tunes language, theme, font, ports and timeouts. An access point without internet never stalls a scan: every resolver lookup has a hard deadline. Silent devices with no open port and no name service stay anonymous.</value></data>
  <data name="aboutTitle"><value>About FluentScanner</value></data>
  <data name="aboutDesc"><value>Finds every device on your LAN: ping plus TCP discovery, open-port sweep, MAC and vendor identification, hostnames.</value></data>
  <data name="aboutOui"><value>Vendor data: IEEE OUI registry.</value></data>
